.TH BOOTSTRAP.SH 1 "2026-09-10" "mu2edaq-shifter-tools" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
bootstrap.sh \- create the Python virtual environment for the shifter tools
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bootstrap.sh
[\fB\-d\fR]
[\fB\-e\fR]
[\fB\-G\fR]
[\fB\-u\fR]
[\fB\-p\fR \fIpython\fR]
[\fB\-f\fR]
[\fB\-h\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B bootstrap.sh
creates \fIvenv/\fR in the installation root and installs the Python
dependencies into it. Python 3.9 or newer is required and the version
is checked before anything is created.
.PP
It also seeds a \fI.env\fR from \fI.env.example\fR if none exists,
never overwriting one that does.
.PP
Only the Python half of the toolkit needs this environment:
.BR daq-read-config (1),
.BR daq-open-tunnels (1),
.BR daq-cluster-cp (1),
.BR daq-ls2json (1)
and
.BR daq-install-tools (1).
The shell commands that read the operations YAML reach it through
.BR daq-read-config (1)
and so need the venv indirectly;
.BR daq-tunnels.sh (1),
.BR manage-vnc-servers.sh (1)
and
.BR start-novnc-connection.sh (1)
have no Python dependency at all and work on a bare laptop.
.PP
.BR start-daq.sh (1)
runs this script automatically when it finds the dependencies missing.
.SH OPTIONS
Configuration precedence is command line, then environment variable,
then built-in default.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-dev
Also install \fBpytest\fR, so the test suite can be run.
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-editable
Also \fBpip install \-e .\fR, which puts the \fBdaq\-*\fR commands on
the venv's PATH. Without it the commands are still reachable, because
the shell wrappers fall back to running the package out of \fIsrc/\fR.
.TP
.BR \-G ", " \-\-no\-gui
Skip PyQt5. Use this on headless DAQ nodes; the only feature lost is
.BR "daq-open-tunnels \-\-gui" .
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-upgrade
Pass \fB\-\-upgrade\fR to pip, so already-installed dependencies are
brought up to date.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-python " " \fIPYTHON\fR
Interpreter used to create the venv. Environment: \fBPYTHON\fR.
Default: \fIpython3\fR.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-force
Delete an existing \fIvenv/\fR and build it again from scratch.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a usage summary and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I requirements.txt
The dependency list installed into the venv.
.TP
.I pyproject.toml
Package metadata, used by \fB\-\-editable\fR.
.TP
.I .env
Created from \fI.env.example\fR on first run.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns 0 on success, 1 if the interpreter is missing or older than
3.9, and 2 for an unrecognised option. A pip failure propagates,
because the script runs under \fBset \-e\fR.
.SH EXAMPLES
Set up for development, with the commands on the PATH and pytest
available:
.PP
.RS
.nf
./bootstrap.sh --dev --editable
source venv/bin/activate
python -m pytest
.fi
.RE
.PP
Set up a headless DAQ node:
.PP
.RS
.nf
./bootstrap.sh --no-gui
.fi
.RE
.PP
Rebuild the environment with a specific interpreter:
.PP
.RS
.nf
./bootstrap.sh --force --python /usr/bin/python3.9
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR install-login.sh (1),
.BR daq-read-config (1),
.BR python3 (1),
.BR pip (1)
